      "id": "wszbbca",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. WHAT IS SUBJECT–VERB AGREEMENT?"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Singular subjects require singular verbs, while plural subjects require plural verbs.",
        "Prepositional phrases placed between a subject and verb do not change the subject's number.",
        "Words like each, every, either, and neither always take a singular verb.",
        "In 'Either...or' and 'Neither...nor' constructs, the verb agrees with the subject closest to it.",
        "Quantities of distance, time, and money are treated as singular concepts."
      ],
      "id": "8lo4pxp"
    },
