      "content": "22. POLITE EXPRESSIONS THAT MISLEAD"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequent SSC Trap: 'A number of' is followed by a plural verb, whereas 'The number of' takes a singular verb.",
        "Watch out for nouns that look plural (e.g., Mathematics, News, Physics) but take singular verbs.",
        "Expressions like 'along with', 'as well as', and 'together with' do not make a singular subject plural."
      ],
      "id": "3yytho7"
